        "content": "Based on the changelog from July 2026 (no August 2026 updates were present), here are the key updates:\n\n## Codex CLI 0.146.0 (July 29, 2026)\nReleased several significant enhancements:\n\n**New capabilities:**\n- Session naming with `/new` or `/clear` commands and thread pinning\n- Support for Agent Plugins manifests and workspace plugin publishing\n- Paginated thread history forking, including temporary forks\n- WebSocket connections to remote Code Mode hosts\n- Standalone web search for compatible custom model providers\n\n**Security improvements:**\n- Comprehensive proxy support across authentication, plugins, MCP, and remote execution\n- Better MCP server connection management and automatic reconnection\n- Strengthened Windows sandboxing with job object process tree termination\n\n**Developer experience:**\n- Improved terminal responsiveness with nonblocking interrupts\n- Better rendering for narrow layouts and hyperlinks\n- Enterprise plan recognition for in-app update controls\n\n## ChatGPT Desktop App 26.727 (July 30, 2026)\nEnhanced browsing, code review, and image editing:\n- Browser address bar for history search and Google queries\n- Multi-repository code review across folders\n- Expanded image viewer with Focused/Canvas views for targeted edits\n- New Activity view in sidebar for recent conversations\n- Chrome extension improvements for YouTube video Q&A\n\n## ChatGPT Voice (July 23, 2026)\nPowered by GPT-Live, enabling voice conversations across Chat, Work, and Codex. Available on macOS with Screen context for appshot sharing.\n\n## Model Retirement (July 31, 2026)\nGPT-5.4 and GPT-5.4 mini will retire from Codex on August 31, 2026. Users should migrate to GPT-5.6 Terra and GPT-5.6 Luna respectively."
